   "start": 1.6,
   "end": 30.7,
   "text": "Just imagine. Your phone buzzes. A WhatsApp group message you have received, and the message is: New IPO opening tomorrow. Grey market premium is ₹120, and it will be a sure-shot listing gain. Your friends have applied, your colleagues have applied. Everybody is talking about it. But fear of missing out is real. But before you put in your hard-earned money, ask the questions a professional analyst asks."
  },
  {
   "src": "/root/.claude/uploads/923aea9c-8345-5808-96a6-1c89f31588ff/5eb58398-9.mkv",
   "asr": "asr/asr9.json",
   "start": 5.35,
   "end": 36.3,
   "text": "So, applying for an IPO just because your grey market premium is high? You should rethink. Grey market premium is an unofficial and unregulated number. There is no exchange, no SEBI oversight and no guarantee. It can be built up in a few days, and it can vanish overnight. Applying only because of grey market premium is not investing. It is all speculation on a WhatsApp rumour. Use GMP, if at all, as a mood indicator. Never a reason."
  },
  {
   "src": "/root/.claude/uploads/923aea9c-8345-5808-96a6-1c89f31588ff/afcd3162-11.mkv",
   "asr": "asr/asr11.json",
   "start": 11.75,
   "end": 17.45,
   "text": "If you cannot answer these questions, then do not apply. There will always be another IPO."
  }
 ],
